OL,3,GNEWSAAberfan falls silent to mark 60
OL,4,Ayears since coal tip collapsed on
OL,5,Aschool and homes, killing 116 children
OL,6,Aand 28 adults
OL,7,
OL,8,FPeople in Aberfan, south Wales, are
OL,9,Fremembering the disaster 60 years ago
OL,10,Fwhen a coal waste tip collapsed on a
OL,11,Fschool and homes
OL,13,FOn 21 October 1966, 116 children and 28
OL,14,Fadults were killed when the colliery
OL,15,Fspoil tip collapsed and engulfed
OL,16,FPantglas Junior School and surrounding
OL,17,Fhouses
OL,19,FOn what was the last day of school
OL,20,Fbefore half term, children were
OL,21,Fsettling down to lessons when tragedy
OL,22,Fstruck
OL,23,APub: 21-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/3
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,432,430,260,140,0,100
